RUNNING MAY

NAME

    may - check, verify and compile May contracts

SYNOPSIS

    cargo run -- help
    cargo run -- check FILE
    cargo run -- verify FILE
    cargo run -- compile FILE

REQUIREMENTS

    Rust
    Cargo
    Z3

The project pins the Rust toolchain. If rustup is installed, cargo should
pick the right compiler for you.

The verifier uses Z3 through the Rust bindings. If the build cannot find Z3,
install it with the system package manager.

On macOS:

    brew install z3

COMMANDS

    cargo run -- help

Print the CLI surface.

    cargo run -- check examples/counter.may

Parse the source and run the semantic pass.

    cargo run -- verify examples/counter.may

Parse, bind and ask the verifier to prove the must bounds and transition.

    cargo run -- compile examples/counter.may

Run the same front end and verifier first. If verification fails, compile does
not write artifacts.

FILES

Successful Algorand compilation writes target output next to the source file:

    examples/build/algorand/

That directory contains:

    approval.teal
    clear.teal
    application.json

NOTES

The generated TEAL is deliberately simple. It dispatches on the first
application argument, updates global state for the supported assignment subset
and rejects calls it does not understand.

EXIT STATUS

    0
        Success.

    non-zero
        Parse errors, semantic errors, verification failures, emission errors
        or file-system errors.
